---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Note from '../components/Note.astro';
import PostPreview from '../components/PostPreview.astro';
import KingsGambit from '../components/KingsGambit.astro';
import CardTrigger from '../components/CardTrigger.astro';
import CardModal from '../components/CardModal.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/agent-profile';
import { pullQuotes, sortedPosts } from '../data/site';

const posts = await sortedPosts();
const recent = posts.slice(0, 6);

const builds = [
  { name: 'saradm.com', href: '/posts/saradmcom-fashion-portfolio-site', line: 'a portfolio and CMS for a fashion stylist, about 1,100 visitors a month' },
  { name: 'ResumeQuiver', href: '/posts/resumequiver', line: 'a resume builder where the resume is YAML and you bring your own AI key' },
  { name: 'Markdown2Paper', href: '/posts/markdown2paper', line: 'an Obsidian plugin that turns notes into formatted papers, built in three hours' },
  { name: 'n8n on NixOS', href: '/posts/nixos', line: 'workflow automation for my father’s small business, without opening my network' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Aurelio Florez">
  <article class="letter col">
    <CardTrigger variant="margin" />
    <p class="lede">I like turning loosely defined problems into systems people can actually use.</p>

    <p>
      This summer, as the AI and operations engineering intern at Melody AV in Miami, that meant a governed,
      read-only bridge into the company’s Sage 100 ERP,<Note n={1}>SageBridge: an MCP server with 12 endpoints
      over 60 approved Sage operations. It replaced about 15 monthly reporting requests that used to mean
      accounting exporting and combining reports by hand. June–July 2026.</Note> an invoice pipeline that reads 23
      vendor formats and matches them to purchase orders,<Note n={2}>In its first 20 days it processed 150 invoices
      and matched 105 of 110 valid ones without intervention, about 26 hours of manual PO checks
      removed.</Note> and sixteen Claude skills for people in finance, sales operations, and field service. I
      onboarded five of them. Four kept using what I built.<Note n={3}>Before the executive reports were released, a 150-run
      evaluation checked them against historical reports written by people. About 130 runs matched the records
      and totals.</Note>
    </p>

    <p>
      At home I run a small NixOS and Libvirt platform on a UPS: isolated VMs for private business software and
      five AI agents, all behind one LiteLLM gateway. One of them is Paquita, my OpenClaw agent, which takes the first
      pass at most of my side projects. It usually gets me 70% of the way; I get it the rest.<Note n={4}>About 110 million tokens a week. The host and
      gateway have run 90 days without an unplanned outage. In a recovery drill SSH was back 19 seconds
      after boot, LiteLLM 36.</Note> Most of what I write comes out of it:
      <a class="link" href="/posts/firecrawl-vs-playwright">what a browser costs an agent</a>,
      <a class="link" href="/posts/tunneling-solutions">how to share a service without sharing the network</a>,
      and <a class="link" href="/posts/nixos-fixing-unstable-packages">what to do when nixpkgs falls behind</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Not everything I try ships. I ran a tracing fork of Hermes Agent on four agents for three weeks. The traces
      made a news-gathering skill better, and the pull request was rejected upstream as too broad.<Note n={5}>Too
      broad and too coupled, fairly. The fork is retired in favor of upstream Hermes and LiteLLM
      observability.</Note> I scope work for coding agents differently now. The smaller fix landed: I diagnosed a
      headless OAuth bug in the same project and wrote the reproductions and regression cases for a fix that
      merged about a day later.<Note n={6}>Another contributor wrote the implementation.
      <a class="link" href="https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/57836" rel="noopener noreferrer">The issue</a>.</Note>
    </p>

    <KingsGambit />
    <p>
      While an agent is thinking, I play chess. Badly: I’m rated around 200, and I open with the King’s Gambit
      because it looks cool. Switching to a browser tab for one-minute blitz wrecked my focus, so I built
      <a class="link" href="/posts/prompt-chess">Prompt-chess</a>, a board that opens in tmux when OpenCode goes
      quiet and disappears when it’s done. The idea was stupid. I knew it was stupid. That’s why I loved it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before Miami I spent almost three years in León, Spain, as a junior developer at i4nm. I moved more than
      150,000 invoices and 10,000 customer records from one ERP to another,<Note n={7}>VisualNT to Holded, with a
      Python utility against the REST API. The team checked every customer and reconciled historical totals
      through year-end reports. 2018–2021.</Note> and wrote a WooCommerce plugin that took stale-inventory refunds
      from about sixty a month to one, across more than fifty stores.
    </p>

    <p>
      Now I’m finishing a computer science degree at FIU and looking for AI, backend, infrastructure, or
      forward-deployed engineering work, close to the people who use what I build. If that sounds like your team,
      <a class="link" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>write to me</a>. The
      <a class="link" href="/resume.pdf">résumé</a> has the short version.
    </p>

    <p class="signoff">Un saludo,<br />Aurelio</p>
    <CardTrigger variant="ps" />
  </article>

  <section class="index col" aria-labelledby="writing">
    <h2 id="writing">Writing</h2>
    <div>
      {recent.map((post) => <PostPreview post={post} quote={pullQuotes[post.id]} />)}
    </div>
    <p class="more"><a class="link" href="/archives">All {posts.length} posts</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="index col" aria-labelledby="built">
    <h2 id="built">Things I’ve built</h2>
    <ul class="builds">
      {builds.map((b) => (
        <li><a class="link" href={b.href}>{b.name}</a>, {b.line}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="more"><a class="link" href="/projects">More on the work page</a></p>
  </section>

  <CardModal />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .letter {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6.5rem);
  }

  .letter > p + p,
  .letter > :global(figure) + p {
    margin-top: 1.05em;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.2vw, 2.05rem);
    line-height: 1.28;
    font-weight: 420;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    margin-bottom: 1.6em;
  }

  .signoff {
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: 1.6em !important;
  }

  .index {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6rem);
  }

  .index h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .builds {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .builds li + li {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
  }

  .more {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
